# Hash-locked tools for the API fuzzing job ONLY (#258).
#
# Kept out of requirements-ci.lock deliberately: Schemathesis pulls in
# hypothesis-jsonschema, starlette, werkzeug and a dozen more, and every one
# of them would then be installed by every cell of the test matrix on every
# OS, to be used by one job on one OS. Scorecard still requires hashes for
# the install, hence a lock of its own -- same arrangement as the mutation
# sweep and the security scan.
#
# The bridge itself is imported by scripts/serve_bridge_for_fuzzing.py, so
# the job also installs requirements-ci.lock; only the fuzzer is here. Both
# locks land in one environment, so every package they share has to agree --
# 21 of them at the time of writing, and the count moves whenever either
# side gains a dependency, which is why the check is a script rather than a
# comment. scripts/lock_conflict_ratchet.py fails the build if two locks
# installed by one job disagree.
# The constraint below is what keeps them agreeing when the lock is
# regenerated: uv reads `-c` out of the input file, so a plain
# `uv pip compile requirements-fuzz.in` -- what the relock workflow runs --
# resolves against the bridge's pins without anyone remembering a flag
# (cubic caught that the first version only passed --constraint by hand).
-c requirements-ci.lock

schemathesis==4.25.2
